{"id":"hamor","name":"Hamor","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:hamor"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hamor","text":"He-ass, a Hivite from whom Jacob purchased the plot of ground in which Joseph was afterwards buried (Gen. 33:19). He is called “Emmor” in Acts 7:16. His son Shechem founded the city of that name which Simeon and Levi destroyed because of his crime in the matter of Dinah, Jacob’s daughter (Gen. 34:20). Hamor and Shechem were also slain (ver. 26)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2544","lemma":"חֲמוֹר","xlit":"Chămôwr","gloss":"Chamor, a Canaanite","kjv":"Hamor","count":4,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H7927","lemma":"שְׁכֶם","xlit":"Shᵉkem","gloss":"Shekem, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Shechem","count":4,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H7192","lemma":"קְשִׂיטָה","xlit":"qᵉsîyṭâh","gloss":"an ingot","kjv":"piece of money","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H2513","lemma":"חֶלְקָה","xlit":"chelqâh","gloss":"smoothness","kjv":"field, flattering, ground, parcel","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H7069","lemma":"קָנָה","xlit":"qânâh","gloss":"to erect","kjv":"attain, buy, teach to keep cattle, get","count":2,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H2026","lemma":"הָרַג","xlit":"hârag","gloss":"to smite with deadly intent","kjv":"destroy, out of hand, kill, murder","count":2,"share":0.33}],"verses":["Gen.33.19","Gen.34.26","Josh.24.32","Judg.9.28","Gen.49.6","Acts.7.16"],"related":[{"id":"shechem","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.042,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"vengeance","type":"lexical","strong":"H2544","why":"both lead with חֲמוֹר (H2544)"},{"id":"shechem","type":"lexical","strong":"H7927","why":"both lead with שְׁכֶם (H7927)"}],"works":[{"work":"antiquities","title":"Antiquities of the Jews","count":2,"chapters":[{"chapter":"AntI.21","count":2,"book":"Ant. 1","title":"Concerning The Violation Of Dina's Chastity."}]},{"work":"philo","title":"The Works of Philo Judaeus","count":2,"chapters":[{"chapter":"PhiloII.2","count"